1022: swap gate for backboardd's asynchronous Metal commits (libm2v, /private/var/tmp/m2v-async-commit).

With the async commit, backboardd's command buffer is submitted by the encode worker after CoreAnimation has
swapped. The flip's GPU gate (0229) snapshots the newest fence at the swap, before the frame's own work exists, so
the frame was flipped undrawn; when an animation stopped the panel kept an older frame (Spotlight half closed).
kern.bergamota_fb_gate_committed / kern.bergamota_fb_gate_submitted (monotonic: a write only raises them) carry backboardd's
commit and submit sequence numbers; a pending swap is taken only once the submits caught up with the commits made
before it, and then the GPU gate waits for a fence snapshotted at that moment. 100 ms cap. Both 0 (no async commit):
no change. Applies after 1021 (boot56); built locally (tools/xnu-local-build.sh --remake), image boot57-swapgate.

